WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.364
The next circle

00:00:01.175 --> 00:00:02.283
of security hell

00:00:02.814 --> 00:00:04.052
A Gentoo developer

00:00:03.864 --> 00:00:04.689
writes about the

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.384
next layer of

00:00:05.196 --> 00:00:06.469
security hardening

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:07.472
and why each

00:00:07.283 --> 00:00:08.627
new defense seems

00:00:08.439 --> 00:00:09.264
to add another

00:00:09.076 --> 00:00:10.549
circle of complexity

00:00:11.086 --> 00:00:12.088
A few years

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:12.795
back I wrote

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:13.927
The modern packager’s

00:00:13.739 --> 00:00:14.953
security nightmare

00:00:15.093 --> 00:00:16.000
In the end

00:00:16.095 --> 00:00:17.627
security is tricky

00:00:18.158 --> 00:00:18.995
The point is

00:00:18.807 --> 00:00:20.374
that nowadays everyone

00:00:20.198 --> 00:00:21.283
and their chatbot

00:00:21.106 --> 00:00:22.945
became security researchers

00:00:23.084 --> 00:00:24.240
On the contrary

00:00:24.405 --> 00:00:25.183
I feel like

00:00:24.995 --> 00:00:26.032
we’re slipping down

00:00:25.844 --> 00:00:27.023
a well-oiled slope

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:27.848
with no end

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.332
in sight

00:00:28.854 --> 00:00:29.868
Full story on

00:00:29.679 --> 00:00:30.575
the dashboard
